<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Bruttium</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Bruttium was the ancient name of the toe of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a>, roughly modern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/calabria">Calabria</a>, named after its people, the Bruttii. Its coasts were lined with Greek cities such as Croton, Locri and Rhegion, while the Oscan-speaking Bruttii held the mountainous interior. It was <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hannibal">Hannibal</a>'s last base in Italy before he left for <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/africa">Africa</a> in 203 BCE.</p></div>
